---
title: "06e  States of one contract, from award to closing"
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  %% QUESTION THIS DIAGRAM ANSWERS: after the award, through which states does a contract pass, which events remove it from the normal path, and which limit applies to each event?
  %% READING: the middle line is the normal path. The states on the sides are the exits and the returns. An arrow without text that returns to "In performance" means that the work continues.
  %% SHORT LABELS: "change within the limit" = an amendment to order (goods) or a variation order (works) of not more than 10 percent of the original contract price, or up to 20 percent with the approval of the head of the procuring entity. "allowed reason" = a reason for suspension or extension that the rules allow. "date passed" = the completion date passed: for each day of delay, damages of one tenth of one percent of the cost of the part that is not performed. "legal ground" = default of the contractor, convenience of the procuring entity (for example when the funding is withheld), unlawful acts, or an event beyond control.
  %% THE ADVANCE: for works, an advance of not more than 15 percent of the contract price, only on the written request of the contractor and against an irrevocable standby letter of credit, a bank guarantee or a surety bond. For goods: 15 percent against a letter of credit or bank guarantee of the same amount. Diagram 07i follows the amounts.
  %% SOURCES: the Implementing Rules of Republic Act No. 12009, text published on 10 February 2025 [IRR12009]: award, contract and securities ss.66-69. Amendment to order and variation order s.71.1.1, s.71.2.1. Suspension and extension s.71.1.2, s.71.2.2, s.71.2.3. Liquidated damages s.71.1.4, s.71.2.4, s.97. Advance payment s.71.1.5, s.71.2.5. Progress payment and retention money s.71.2.7, s.71.2.8. Termination s.71.4. Warranty s.90. Sanctions ss.98-105. Period for the notice to proceed [RA12009 s.66]. Multi-year contracts need a Multi-Year Contractual Authority [IRR12009 s.9][CL2025-6]. No payment before a certificate that the delivery was inspected and accepted, except an approved advance [PD1445 s.88].
  %% A DIFFERENCE INSIDE THE RULES: for goods, the damages are counted on the cost of the delayed goods [IRR12009 s.71.1.4]. The general rule counts them on the cost of the unperformed portion [IRR12009 s.97].
  %% LIMIT: later amendments of the Rules are not in the text that I read. The Rules leave other details of contract implementation to manuals of the GPPB, which I did not open [IRR12009 s.71.1.6].

  state "Awarded" as AW
  state "Performance security provided" as PS
  state "Contract signed, obligation recorded" as SG
  state "Notice to proceed issued" as NTP
  state "Advance paid against a security" as ADV
  state "In performance" as PERF
  state "Delivery or work claimed (billing)" as CL
  state "Inspected and accepted, or work certified" as ACC
  state "Paid (partial or final)" as PAID
  state "Warranty or defects liability period" as WAR
  state "Closed, retention money and securities released" as CLOSED
  state "Changed (amendment or variation order)" as VAR
  state "Suspended, or time extended" as SUSP
  state "In delay, liquidated damages apply" as DELAY
  state "Terminated" as TERM
  state "Contractor suspended or blacklisted" as BL
  state "Rejected, to be corrected" as REJ

  [*] --> AW: head of the procuring entity issues the notice of award
  AW --> PS: winning bidder, 5 or 10 percent of the contract price
  PS --> SG: within 10 days from receipt of the notice of award
  SG --> NTP: within 3 days from approval of the contract
  NTP --> PERF: contractor starts
  NTP --> ADV: written request and security (see header)
  ADV --> PERF
  PERF --> CL: contractor delivers, or bills the work done (works, once a month)
  CL --> ACC: inspection and acceptance, or certificate of the engineer of the agency
  CL --> REJ: delivery does not meet the contract
  REJ --> CL: contractor corrects
  ACC --> PAID: voucher, payment order (chapter 07), less advance recovered and retention money
  PAID --> PERF: more to deliver
  PAID --> WAR: last delivery accepted, or works completed
  WAR --> CLOSED: period ends without defect, or defects repaired
  PERF --> VAR: change within the limit
  VAR --> PERF
  PERF --> SUSP: allowed reason
  SUSP --> PERF
  PERF --> DELAY: date passed
  DELAY --> CL: late delivery
  DELAY --> TERM: damages reach 10 percent of the contract price
  PERF --> TERM: legal ground
  TERM --> BL: grounds proven
  WAR --> BL: defects not repaired within 90 days
  CLOSED --> [*]
  TERM --> [*]
  BL --> [*]
